{"agent":"par-kilo","data":{"budget":"","claim":"A descriptor's agent-specific Python is exactly its hook normalizer and emitter; it is bespoke iff one of them is used by no OTHER descriptor, and the shipped 24 descriptors grade bespoke as {antigravity, cline, copilot, cursor, goose, windsurf}.","falsifier":"Two descriptors with the same fact names but different stdin paths must grade TWO distinct normalizers: grade them as SHARED (facts-only signature) and the signature is wrong.","item":"PAR-data-first","mechanism":"usage() counts each normalizer and emitter over the hooked descriptors; a key used by <2 descriptors is bespoke. Two descriptors with an identical field map share one normalizer; an empty map is the shared default.","probe":"run ddflow.services.parity.reuse.measure() and print bespoke, normalizer_bespoke, emitter_bespoke, zero_python","probe_output":"agents=24 hooked=19 zero_python=18 rate=0.75 bespoke=[antigravity,cline,copilot,cursor,goose,windsurf]; emitter-only proxy (harness_conformance.report.zero_python) = 20/24 bespoke=[antigravity,cline,copilot,cursor]","question":"Which descriptors need per-agent Python, given only their hook normalizer ([hooks.fields]) and emitter ([hooks] emit variant), and can that measure be a first-class report with a shrink-only ratchet?","sources":[],"verdict":"CONFIRMED"},"id":"e81c62ac2b38b29bb249c4c29","kind":"research.recorded","lamport":178037,"schema":1,"subject":"R4bb6ab9a5f","ts":"2026-11-11T22:14:34.062756Z"}
