{"agent":"par-kilo","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"The ratchet does not enforce the contract this change exists for. `test_the_bespoke_set_only_shrinks` and `R.unrecorded(recorded=BASELINE)` only compare agent ids to `BASELINE`. A new descriptor whose normalizer or emitter is used by nobody else, with an empty or missing driver delta note, still passes once its id is added to `BASELINE` (and `test_unrecorded` returns `[]` for `recorded=frozenset({\"novel\"})` with no note at all). The module comment and the test docstring claim that case must fail until the gap is recorded with a reason.","digest":"0c55e54f3fe8e441","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_parity_reuse.py:90","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_parity_reuse.py:90"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"`delta_note` joins `h.delta` onto `DELTA_DIR` and treats any non-empty read as a recorded gap. `Path` replaces the base when the right-hand side is absolute, and `..` is honored by `read_text`, so the check is not confined to `templates/drivers/deltas`. A bespoke harness with `delta=\"/etc/hostname\"` (or `delta=\"../some-nonempty.txt\"`) and `recorded={\"novel\"}` makes `unrecorded` return `[]` even though no driver delta note exists; the ratchet the change adds is bypassed by the path in the descriptor field, not by a note that states the gap and its reason.","digest":"677d4bc8f378ef60","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/parity/reuse.py:141","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/parity/reuse.py:141"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_findings":1,"delta_from":"330708927249e543d60af500b7f08b2cb2fb164f","delta_raised":["677d4bc8f378ef60"],"delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":4496,"diff_sha":"49c9d86344c5a3f5aac7dec34fd473c5e8637ba9ca1c55b0faa05a813acaad4f","diff_source":"delta review of 1 commit since 3307089272","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"unt